reason: >
  src/chebyshev.cpp line ~419: verbose >= 2 emits diagnostics only at iter == 0
  (the initial iterate), not at each IPM iteration. No per-IPM-iteration trajectory
  is available without adding instrumentation to the solver internals, which is
  forbidden by task constraints (no src/ edits). Trajectory analysis is therefore
  structurally impossible without solver modification.
impact: >
  Cause attribution proceeds via single-thread vs multi-thread weight comparison
  (d_st vs d_mt) as specified. Trajectory data is not needed for cause (c)
  resolution: d_st = 2.047e-3 > 1e-3 at single-thread confirms shared-code
  numerical drift independent of thread count.
